    "Every paper is a Computer Engineering paper with 15 questions: five 5-mark questions in Q1 and ten 10-mark questions in Q2 to Q6, two per question.",
    "Cloud computing models are asked in 5 of 6 papers. Impact of IT and IS on organizations and society is asked 6 times, and data warehouse and data mart 4 times across 4 papers.",
    "Cyber security measures with example is asked 4 times in 3 papers, once as a duplicate on the December 2024 paper. It is a safe 10-mark answer to prepare.",
    "Many 10-mark questions repeat word for word in later papers (Big Data challenges, CRM types, e-commerce note, knowledge capturing), so the solved past papers cover most of what comes.",
    "Q1 spreads across modules: social computing, is-fundamentals, SDLC and business intelligence appear most often among the 5-mark parts, and the SDLC tools question repeats in 3 papers."
